module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.Basic

/-!
# The irrelevant finite graded modules form a Serre subcategory

Let `A` be a graded ring and let `d` be a positive integer — in the source, the least common
multiple of the degrees of a chosen finite set of homogeneous generators of `A` over `A₀` of
positive degree. Following Stacks 0BXE, a homogeneous element `x` of a graded `A`-module `M`
is *irrelevant* when `(A₊ x)_{nd} = 0` for all `n ≫ 0`, and `M` is irrelevant when all of its
homogeneous elements are. Those modules are `Mod^{fg}_{A, irrelevant}` once one restricts to
the finitely generated graded modules, and Tag 0BXF is the assertion that `M ↦ M̃` induces an
equivalence `Mod^{fg}_A / Mod^{fg}_{A, irrelevant} ⟶ Coh(𝒪_X)` for `X = Proj(A)` and `A`
Noetherian, with quasi-inverse `ℱ ↦ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))`.

This file proves the step of that proposition which makes its statement meaningful: the
irrelevant finitely generated graded modules satisfy the Serre-subcategory condition of
Stacks 02MO, so that the quotient category in the statement exists. The equivalence itself is
not proved here; see "What is missing" below.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.IsIrrelevantElement` — the source's
  irrelevant homogeneous element: `(A₊ x)_{nd} = 0` for all large `n`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.IsIrrelevant` — the source's irrelevant
  graded module, `M_{irrelevant} = M`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.GradeEventuallyZero` — the condition
  `M_{nd} = 0` for all large `n`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.FiniteGradedModules` — the category
  `Mod^{fg}_A` of finitely generated graded `A`-modules.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.irrelevantModules` — the full subcategory
  `Mod^{fg}_{A, irrelevant}` of it, as an `ObjectProperty`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.gradeComponent` — the additive projection
  of a graded module onto one of its homogeneous pieces.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.isIrrelevant_iff_gradeEventuallyZero` —
  the source's parenthetical identification: a *finitely generated* graded module is
  irrelevant exactly when `M_{nd} = 0` for all large `n`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.isIrrelevant_of_exact` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.irrelevantModules_prop_of_exact` — the
  Serre-subcategory condition: the middle term of an exact sequence of finitely generated
  graded modules whose outer terms are irrelevant is irrelevant.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_gradeEventuallyZero`
  — an irrelevant module is killed, on each homogeneous element whose degree is a multiple of
  `deg f`, by a power of every homogeneous `f` of positive degree. This is the vanishing of the
  spanning fractions of the degree-zero localization `M₍f₎`, hence of the sections of `M̃` over
  the standard open `D₊(f)`.

## Implementation notes

The condition proved is the one Stacks 02MO states — nonempty, and containing the middle term
of every exact sequence whose outer terms belong to it — rather than Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsSerreClass`. The two agree by
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isSerreClass_iff_prop_X₂_of_exact` (Tag 02MP), but only in an
*abelian* category, and `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality.GradedModuleCat` — the
category of graded modules this library has — carries no abelian structure yet. Exactness is
therefore spelled elementwise, as the inclusion of the kernel of the second map in the image of
the first, which is the half of exactness at the middle term that the condition consumes.

The degree `d` is a parameter rather than the least common multiple of the degrees of a chosen
generating set: every statement below holds for each positive `d`, so in particular for the
source's. No Noetherian hypothesis is used, and finite generation is assumed only where the
source uses it, in `isIrrelevant_iff_gradeEventuallyZero` and downstream of it.

The hard half of that identification is where finite generation enters. A finitely generated
graded module is generated by the finitely many homogeneous components of a finite generating
set, and each of them is irrelevant with its own bound; the maximum of those finitely many
bounds, pushed past the largest degree occurring among them, is a bound that works for the
whole module. Writing an element of `M_{nd}` as an `A`-combination of those generators and
taking degree-`nd` components kills every term, because the coefficient needed in each term is
homogeneous of positive degree.

### What is missing

Tag 0BXF itself — the equivalence — is not formalized. Its remaining inputs, none of which
this library has, are: exactness of `M ↦ M̃` (part of Tag 01M7), the identification of the
kernel of that functor with the irrelevant modules, Tag 0B5Q (finiteness of
`⨁_{d ≥ k} H⁰(X, ℱ(d))` over `A`), Tag 0B5R (the comparison maps `N → N'` and `M → N'` and
their behaviour in large degrees), and Tag 0AG5 (the canonical map `M̃ → ℱ` is an isomorphism).
The quasi-inverse `ℱ ↦ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` also has no functorial form here:
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistedGlobalSections` is `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} Γ(X, ℱ(n))`
with its graded module structure, but its nonnegative part is not cut out, it is not known to
be finitely generated, and it is not assembled into a functor out of `Coh(𝒪_X)` — for which
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.CoherentModules` of the `Proj` structure sheaf is the category.

What *is* available towards the kernel identification is
`exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_gradeEventuallyZero` above: it kills every spanning fraction of
`GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization`, so `M₍f₎ = 0` for each homogeneous `f` of positive
degree. Turning that into `M̃ = 0` needs the standard opens to cover `Proj(A)` together with
the separation property of the sheaf, neither of which is assembled here; and the converse
direction, `M̃ = 0 ⟹ M` irrelevant, is the one that needs Tag 0B5R.

That last gap is not filled by the theorem
`isZero_associatedModuleSheaf_of_eventually_eq_zero` of this same namespace, in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.TorsionVanishing`, which proves
`M̃ = 0` by showing every *fiber* `M_𝔭` is trivial. That argument needs the components of `M` to
vanish in all large degrees, which is `d = 1` — the degree-one generated case of Tag 0BXD. For
`d > 1` the fibers of an irrelevant module need not be trivial, only the degree-zero parts of
its localizations, so the vanishing has to be read off the sections rather than the fibers; the
lemma above is the degree-zero form the sections need.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02MO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory DirectSum
open Stacks.GradedLocalization
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSheafFunctoriality

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence

universe u v w

variable {S : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮]

/-- The projection of a graded module onto its degree-`j` homogeneous piece, as an additive
map. It is additive but not `S`-linear: multiplying by a homogeneous scalar shifts degrees. -/
public def gradeComponent (M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮) (j : ℤ) :
    M.carrier →+ M.grade j :=
  (DFinsupp.evalAddMonoidHom j).comp
    (DirectSum.decomposeAddEquiv M.grade).toAddMonoidHom

/-- The degree-`j` component of `x`, viewed in the module, is `decompose M.grade x j`. -/
@[simp] public theorem gradeComponent_apply (M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮) (j : ℤ)
    (x : M.carrier) :
    (gradeComponent 𝒮 M j x : M.carrier) = (DirectSum.decompose M.grade x j : M.carrier) := rfl

/-- A homogeneous element is its own component in its own degree. -/
public theorem gradeComponent_of_mem_same {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} {j : ℤ}
    {x : M.carrier} (hx : x ∈ M.grade j) : (gradeComponent 𝒮 M j x : M.carrier) = x :=
  DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_same _ hx

/-- A homogeneous element has no component in any other degree. -/
public theorem gradeComponent_of_mem_ne {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} {i j : ℤ}
    {x : M.carrier} (hx : x ∈ M.grade i) (hij : i ≠ j) :
    (gradeComponent 𝒮 M j x : M.carrier) = 0 :=
  DirectSum.decompose_of_mem_ne _ hx hij

/-- An element of a vanishing homogeneous piece is zero. -/
public theorem eq_zero_of_mem_grade_eq_bot {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} {j : ℤ}
    (h : M.grade j = ⊥) {y : M.carrier} (hy : y ∈ M.grade j) : y = 0 := by
  rw [h] at hy
  simpa using hy

/-- A degree-preserving map commutes with taking homogeneous components. -/
public theorem gradeComponent_map {M N : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} (f : M ⟶ N) (j : ℤ)
    (x : M.carrier) :
    (gradeComponent 𝒮 N j (f.toLinearMap x) : N.carrier) =
      f.toLinearMap (gradeComponent 𝒮 M j x : M.carrier) := by
  classical
  have hx : ∑ i ∈ (DirectSum.decompose M.grade x).support,
      ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade x) i : M.carrier) = x :=
    DirectSum.sum_support_decompose M.grade x
  conv_lhs => rw [← hx]
  rw [map_sum, map_sum]
  push_cast
  by_cases hj : j ∈ (DirectSum.decompose M.grade x).support
  · rw [Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem j hj (fun i _ hij =>
      gradeComponent_of_mem_ne 𝒮 (f.map_grade i _ ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade x) i).2) hij)]
    exact gradeComponent_of_mem_same 𝒮
      (f.map_grade j _ ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade x) j).2)
  · have hzero : ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade x) j : M.carrier) = 0 := by
      rw [DFinsupp.notMem_support_iff.1 hj]
      rfl
    have hne : ∀ i ∈ (DirectSum.decompose M.grade x).support, i ≠ j :=
      fun i hi h => hj (by rw [← h]; exact hi)
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun i hi => gradeComponent_of_mem_ne 𝒮
      (f.map_grade i _ ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade x) i).2) (hne i hi))]
    simp [gradeComponent_apply, hzero]

/-- **Stacks 0BXE.** A homogeneous element `x` of degree `i` of a graded `A`-module is
*irrelevant* for the degree `d` when `(A₊ x)_{nd} = 0` for all sufficiently large `n`: every
homogeneous element of `A` of positive degree `k` with `k + i = nd` and `n` large kills `x`. -/
public def IsIrrelevantElement (d : ℕ) (M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮) (i : ℤ)
    (x : M.carrier) : Prop :=
  ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n → ∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → (k : ℤ) + i = (n : ℤ) * d → ∀ a ∈ 𝒮 k, a • x = 0

/-- **Stacks 0BXE.** A graded module is *irrelevant* when `M_{irrelevant} = M`, that is, when
every homogeneous element of it is irrelevant. -/
public def IsIrrelevant (d : ℕ) (M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮) : Prop :=
  ∀ (i : ℤ) (x : M.carrier), x ∈ M.grade i → IsIrrelevantElement 𝒮 d M i x

/-- The condition `M_{nd} = 0` for all large `n`, which the source uses as the working form of
irrelevance for finitely generated modules. -/
@[ega "II 3.4.2"]
public def GradeEventuallyZero (d : ℕ) (M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮) : Prop :=
  ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n → M.grade ((n : ℤ) * d) = ⊥

/-- A module vanishing in all large degrees divisible by `d` is irrelevant. -/
public theorem isIrrelevant_of_gradeEventuallyZero {d : ℕ} {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮}
    (h : GradeEventuallyZero 𝒮 d M) : IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d M := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := h
  intro i x hx
  refine ⟨N, fun n hn k hk hki a ha => ?_⟩
  have hmem : a • x ∈ M.grade ((k : ℤ) + i) := SetLike.GradedSMul.smul_mem ha hx
  rw [hki] at hmem
  exact eq_zero_of_mem_grade_eq_bot 𝒮 (hN n hn) hmem

/-- Every `S`-multiple of a homogeneous element `x` of degree `i` has zero component in a
degree `j > i` into which no homogeneous scalar can carry `x`. -/
public theorem gradeComponent_smul_eq_zero {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} {i j : ℤ}
    {x : M.carrier} (hx : x ∈ M.grade i) (hij : i < j)
    (hkill : ∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k → (k : ℤ) + i = j → ∀ a ∈ 𝒮 k, a • x = 0) (r : S) :
    (gradeComponent 𝒮 M j (r • x) : M.carrier) = 0 := by
  classical
  have hr : ∑ k ∈ (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 r).support,
      ((DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 r) k : S) = r := DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒮 r
  have hsmul : r • x = ∑ k ∈ (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 r).support,
      (((DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 r) k : S)) • x := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_smul, hr]
  rw [hsmul, map_sum]
  push_cast
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun k _ => ?_
  by_cases hk : (k : ℤ) + i = j
  · have hk0 : 0 < k := by omega
    rw [hkill k hk0 hk _ (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 r k).2]
    simp
  · exact gradeComponent_of_mem_ne 𝒮
      (SetLike.GradedSMul.smul_mem (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 r k).2 hx) hk

/-- An irrelevant *finitely generated* graded module vanishes in all large degrees divisible
by `d`. This is the half of the source's parenthetical identification that uses finite
generation. -/
public theorem gradeEventuallyZero_of_isIrrelevant {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} [Module.Finite S M.carrier]
    (h : IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d M) : GradeEventuallyZero 𝒮 d M := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : (⊤ : Submodule S M.carrier).FG := Module.Finite.fg_top
  set G : Finset (ℤ × M.carrier) :=
    s.biUnion (fun y => (DirectSum.decompose M.grade y).support.image
      (fun i => (i, ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade y) i : M.carrier)))) with hG
  have hGmem : ∀ p ∈ G, p.2 ∈ M.grade p.1 := by
    intro p hp
    simp only [hG, Finset.mem_biUnion, Finset.mem_image] at hp
    obtain ⟨y, -, i, -, rfl⟩ := hp
    exact ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade y) i).2
  have hspan : Submodule.span S
      ((G.image Prod.snd : Finset M.carrier) : Set M.carrier) = ⊤ := by
    refine le_antisymm le_top ?_
    rw [← hs]
    refine Submodule.span_le.2 fun y hy => ?_
    rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose M.grade y]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i hi => Submodule.subset_span ?_
    simp only [Finset.coe_image, Set.mem_image, Finset.mem_coe]
    exact ⟨(i, ((DirectSum.decompose M.grade y) i : M.carrier)), by
      simp only [hG, Finset.mem_biUnion, Finset.mem_image]
      exact ⟨y, hy, i, hi, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  have hb : ∀ p ∈ G, ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n → ∀ k : ℕ, 0 < k →
      (k : ℤ) + p.1 = (n : ℤ) * d → ∀ a ∈ 𝒮 k, a • p.2 = 0 :=
    fun p hp => h p.1 p.2 (hGmem p hp)
  choose! bd hbd using hb
  refine ⟨max (G.sup bd) (G.sup (fun p => p.1.toNat) + 1), fun n hn => ?_⟩
  have hn1 : G.sup bd ≤ n := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) hn
  have hn2 : G.sup (fun p => p.1.toNat) + 1 ≤ n := le_trans (le_max_right _ _) hn
  have hdeg : ∀ p ∈ G, p.1 < (n : ℤ) * d := by
    intro p hp
    have h1 : p.1 ≤ ((G.sup (fun q : ℤ × M.carrier => q.1.toNat) : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
      have := Finset.le_sup (f := fun q : ℤ × M.carrier => q.1.toNat) hp
      omega
    have h2 : (n : ℤ) * 1 ≤ (n : ℤ) * d := by
      have hd' : (1 : ℤ) ≤ (d : ℤ) := by exact_mod_cast hd
      exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hd' (by positivity)
    have h3 : ((G.sup (fun q : ℤ × M.carrier => q.1.toNat) : ℕ) : ℤ) < (n : ℤ) := by
      exact_mod_cast hn2
    omega
  rw [eq_bot_iff]
  intro m hm
  have hmtop : m ∈ Submodule.span S
      ((G.image Prod.snd : Finset M.carrier) : Set M.carrier) := by
    rw [hspan]; trivial
  rw [Submodule.mem_span_finset] at hmtop
  obtain ⟨f, -, hf⟩ := hmtop
  have hzero : (gradeComponent 𝒮 M ((n : ℤ) * d) m : M.carrier) = 0 := by
    rw [← hf, map_sum]
    push_cast
    refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x hx => ?_
    simp only [Finset.mem_image] at hx
    obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact gradeComponent_smul_eq_zero 𝒮 (hGmem p hp) (hdeg p hp)
      (fun k hk hki a ha =>
        hbd p hp n (le_trans (Finset.le_sup (f := bd) hp) hn1) k hk hki a ha) (f p.2)
  rw [gradeComponent_of_mem_same 𝒮 hm] at hzero
  simpa using hzero

/-- **Stacks 0BXE.** For a finitely generated graded module, the source's irrelevance — every
homogeneous element irrelevant — is the same as vanishing in all large degrees divisible by
`d`. -/
public theorem isIrrelevant_iff_gradeEventuallyZero {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} [Module.Finite S M.carrier] :
    IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d M ↔ GradeEventuallyZero 𝒮 d M :=
  ⟨gradeEventuallyZero_of_isIrrelevant 𝒮 hd, isIrrelevant_of_gradeEventuallyZero 𝒮⟩

/-- A zero graded module is irrelevant. -/
public theorem isIrrelevant_of_subsingleton {d : ℕ} {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮}
    [Subsingleton M.carrier] : IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d M :=
  fun _ _ _ => ⟨0, fun _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => Subsingleton.elim _ _⟩

/-- The Serre-subcategory condition of Stacks 02MO for the irrelevant modules. Let
`L → N → P` be maps of finitely generated graded modules with the kernel of `N → P` contained
in the image of `L → N`. If `L` and `P` are irrelevant then so is `N`. -/
public theorem isIrrelevant_of_exact {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    {L N P : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} [Module.Finite S L.carrier]
    [Module.Finite S P.carrier] (f : L ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ P)
    (hexact : ∀ y : N.carrier, g.toLinearMap y = 0 → ∃ x : L.carrier, f.toLinearMap x = y)
    (hL : IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d L) (hP : IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d P) : IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d N := by
  obtain ⟨N₁, hN₁⟩ := gradeEventuallyZero_of_isIrrelevant 𝒮 hd hL
  obtain ⟨N₂, hN₂⟩ := gradeEventuallyZero_of_isIrrelevant 𝒮 hd hP
  refine isIrrelevant_of_gradeEventuallyZero 𝒮 ⟨max N₁ N₂, fun n hn => ?_⟩
  have hn1 : N₁ ≤ n := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) hn
  have hn2 : N₂ ≤ n := le_trans (le_max_right _ _) hn
  rw [eq_bot_iff]
  intro y hy
  have hgy : g.toLinearMap y = 0 :=
    eq_zero_of_mem_grade_eq_bot 𝒮 (hN₂ n hn2) (g.map_grade _ y hy)
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hexact y hgy
  have hxc : (gradeComponent 𝒮 L ((n : ℤ) * d) x : L.carrier) = 0 :=
    eq_zero_of_mem_grade_eq_bot 𝒮 (hN₁ n hn1) (gradeComponent 𝒮 L ((n : ℤ) * d) x).2
  have hyc : y = f.toLinearMap (gradeComponent 𝒮 L ((n : ℤ) * d) x : L.carrier) := by
    rw [← gradeComponent_map 𝒮 f, hx, gradeComponent_of_mem_same 𝒮 hy]
  rw [hxc, map_zero] at hyc
  simpa using hyc

/-- A module vanishing in all large degrees divisible by `D` is power-torsion for every
homogeneous element of positive degree, on the homogeneous elements whose degree is a multiple
of that of the element. This is the generator-level statement that the degree-zero localization
`M₍f₎` — the sections of `M̃` over the standard open `D₊(f)`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.associatedModuleSheafStandardOpenEquiv` — vanishes,
since `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.GradedModuleDegreeZeroLocalization` is spanned
by the fractions `x / f ^ n` with `x` of degree `n · deg f`. -/
public theorem exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_gradeEventuallyZero {D : ℕ} (hD : 0 < D)
    {M : GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮} (h : GradeEventuallyZero 𝒮 D M)
    {k : ℕ} (hk : 0 < k) {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 k) {n : ℕ} {x : M.carrier}
    (hx : x ∈ M.grade ((n : ℤ) * k)) : ∃ j : ℕ, f ^ j • x = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := h
  refine ⟨D * (N + n) - n, ?_⟩
  have hle : n ≤ D * (N + n) :=
    le_trans (Nat.le_add_left n N) (Nat.le_mul_of_pos_left _ hD)
  have hjn : n + (D * (N + n) - n) = D * (N + n) := by omega
  have hfj : f ^ (D * (N + n) - n) ∈ 𝒮 ((D * (N + n) - n) * k) := by
    simpa [smul_eq_mul] using SetLike.pow_mem_graded (D * (N + n) - n) hf
  have hmem : f ^ (D * (N + n) - n) • x ∈
      M.grade ((((D * (N + n) - n) * k : ℕ) : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) * k) :=
    SetLike.GradedSMul.smul_mem hfj hx
  have hdeg : (((D * (N + n) - n) * k : ℕ) : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) * k = (((N + n) * k : ℕ) : ℤ) * D := by
    have : ((D * (N + n) - n : ℕ) : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) = ((D * (N + n) : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
      push_cast [hle]
      omega
    push_cast at this ⊢
    nlinarith [this]
  rw [hdeg] at hmem
  refine eq_zero_of_mem_grade_eq_bot 𝒮 (hN ((N + n) * k) ?_) hmem
  calc N ≤ N + n := Nat.le_add_right _ _
    _ ≤ (N + n) * k := Nat.le_mul_of_pos_right _ hk

/-- The category `Mod^{fg}_A` of finitely generated graded `A`-modules of Tag 0BXE. -/
public abbrev FiniteGradedModules : Type _ :=
  ObjectProperty.FullSubcategory
    (C := GradedModuleCat.{u, v, w} 𝒮) (fun M => Module.Finite S M.carrier)

/-- The full subcategory `Mod^{fg}_{A, irrelevant}` of the irrelevant finitely generated
graded modules, as an `ObjectProperty` of `Mod^{fg}_A`. -/
public def irrelevantModules (d : ℕ) :
    ObjectProperty (FiniteGradedModules.{u, v, w} 𝒮) := fun M => IsIrrelevant 𝒮 d M.obj

/-- The irrelevant finitely generated graded modules satisfy the Serre-subcategory condition of
Stacks 02MO inside `Mod^{fg}_A`: they contain every zero module, and they contain the middle term
of every exact sequence whose outer terms belong to them. -/
@[stacks 0BXF "only the step that the irrelevant finite graded modules satisfy the \
Serre-subcategory condition of Tag 02MO, which is what makes the quotient category in the \
statement exist; the equivalence with Coh(O_X) and its twisted-section quasi-inverse are not \
formalized, and exactness is spelled elementwise because this library's category of graded \
modules has no abelian structure yet"]
public theorem irrelevantModules_prop_of_exact {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    (M₀ : FiniteGradedModules.{u, v, w} 𝒮) (h₀ : Subsingleton M₀.obj.carrier) :
    irrelevantModules 𝒮 d M₀ ∧
      ∀ (L N P : FiniteGradedModules.{u, v, w} 𝒮) (f : L ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ P),
        (∀ y : N.obj.carrier, g.hom.toLinearMap y = 0 →
          ∃ x : L.obj.carrier, f.hom.toLinearMap x = y) →
        irrelevantModules 𝒮 d L → irrelevantModules 𝒮 d P → irrelevantModules 𝒮 d N :=
  ⟨@isIrrelevant_of_subsingleton _ _ _ _ _ 𝒮 _ d M₀.obj h₀,
    fun L N P f g hexact hL hP =>
      @isIrrelevant_of_exact _ _ _ _ _ 𝒮 _ d hd L.obj N.obj P.obj L.property P.property
        f.hom g.hom hexact hL hP⟩

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence

end
